class.description:
Reach it through [member NetwEntity.simulation]. It is never [code]null[/code], and there is one per entity.
Each peer resolves one [member mode] for the entity. The body's freeze, the [member step], how an arriving sample lands and how the entity is drawn all follow that mode. A game writes the declaration below and reads the mode, and never writes the mode.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _init() -> void:
    var entity := Netw.configure_entity(self)
    entity.simulation.bodies = [^"Sphere"]
    entity.simulation.replicas = NetwSimulationHandle.REPLICAS_ACTIVE

func _network_tick(delta: float, tick: int, is_fresh: bool) -> void:
    if is_fresh:
        steer(delta)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public Car()
{
    var entity = Netw.ConfigureEntity(this);
    entity.Simulation.Bodies = new Godot.Collections.Array { new NodePath("Sphere") };
    entity.Simulation.Replicas = NetwSimulationHandle.ReplicasEnum.Active;
    entity.Simulation.Step = Callable.From<double, long, bool>(Step);
}

private void Step(double delta, long tick, bool isFresh)
{
    if (isFresh)
        Steer(delta);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
An entity is simulated when it writes any member here, calls a selection method, declares [member NetwPredictionHandle.archetype], or has a [RigidBody2D] or [RigidBody3D] root that [member NetwEntity.interpolation] draws. Every other entity stays [constant MODE_NONE] on every peer.
[b]Modes[/b]
The peer that authors the entity runs it as [constant MODE_AUTHORITY]. A controller running a predicted entity ahead runs it as [constant MODE_PREDICT]. Every other copy is [constant MODE_PROXY], frozen and drawn from history, unless [member replicas] or a selection makes it [constant MODE_ACTIVE].
[codeblock lang=text]
mode       the step           the body
AUTHORITY  runs               runs with the settings the scene authored
PREDICT    runs and replays   runs with the settings the scene authored
ACTIVE     runs, never fresh  runs, and installs each sample it receives
PROXY      does not run       frozen kinematic, drawn from history
NONE       does not run       untouched
[/codeblock]
An [constant MODE_ACTIVE] copy that touches a body this peer runs as [constant MODE_AUTHORITY] or [constant MODE_PREDICT] keeps its own response to the touch. It skips every sample the author sent before the touch, and the author's later samples correct it as usual. One of the two bodies must report contacts through [member RigidBody3D.contact_monitor].
[b]Selection[/b]
While this entity runs here as [constant MODE_AUTHORITY] or [constant MODE_PREDICT], it can pick other entities to run here as [constant MODE_ACTIVE]. [method simulate] names one, and [method simulate_nearest], [method simulate_within] and [method simulate_all] set one automatic policy, which the last call replaces. A change takes effect at the start of the next tick.
[codeblock]
func _ready() -> void:
    entity.simulation.simulate(ball)
    entity.simulation.simulate_nearest(2, &"arena")
[/codeblock]
An entity named with [method simulate] never spends the automatic policy's budget. A predicted entity keeps an entity it selected while the two touch. The selection belongs to this handle, so it holds across prediction being declared again.
